      "content": "While his stated preference for structure might seem like a speed bump, consider if his \"steady\" approach actually translates to strategic reliability under pressure, which can prevent costly, unplanned chaos. Look for evidence of successful disruption in his history, perhaps where he streamlined a highly volatile project rather than just managing the pace. If you can't find direct evidence of \"controlled chaos tolerance,\" the risk of a misaligned pace is substantial for a high-stakes role.",
